Advancing DevSecOps Maturity
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

• Understand the fundamental concepts of DevSecOps and its importance in modern software development • Set up a complete CI/CD pipeline using open-source tools • Integrate security scanning tools into the development workflow • Configure automated security testing at multiple stages of the pipeline • Implement Infrastructure as Code (IaC) security scanning • Monitor and analyze security metrics in a DevSecOps environment • Apply best practices for secure code development and deployment

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

• Basic understanding of Linux command line operations • Familiarity with Git version control concepts • Basic knowledge of Docker containers • Understanding of software development lifecycle • No prior DevSecOps experience required - this lab is designed for beginners

